.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SS "template<uint32_t dim>
.br
class csmp::PoreVolumeVisitor< dim >"Calculating the volume and pore volume of a node-centered control volume\&.

.PP
\fBAuthor\fP
.RS 4
Philipp Weis, ETH Zuerich 
.RE
.PP
.SH "Contact"
.PP
philipp.weis@erdw.ethz.ch

.PP
@changes changes Latest Changes
.SH "Motivation"
.PP
Intitially designed to avoid the usage of the FiniteVolumeManager in csp5\&. Output as nodal field variables allows to use them for post-processing (e\&.g\&. with ParaView or MatLab)\&.
.SH "Usage"
.PP
Used within the CVFEM scheme (Weis et al\&., Geofluids, 2014)\&.

.PP
.PP
.nf
The visitor reads in a nodal variable for porosity, which has to be initialised before visitation
It further requires existing nodal variables for volume and pore volume\&.
The three variable names are provided as constructor arguments\&.

  The visitor calculates the node\-centered volume and pore volume, assuming that all elements contribute equally to the control volumes of their respecetive nodes\&.

The values for volume and pore volume are stored as nodal variables\&.
.fi
.PP
.SH "Dependencies"
.PP
.SH "Known issues"
.PP
There may be new funcionality in CSMP++ that could make this visitor redundant\&. Only \fBVisit(Node<dim>* n)\fP is overwritten\&. However, application target and level are always set to NODE\&. How to limit to \fBRegion\fP (former Group)?

.PP
Does the Application Level have to be changed? How can it be restricted to a \fBRegion\fP? Include the possibility to use porosity as an element variable? Change name to NodalPoreVolumeVisitor?
.SH "Testing"
.PP
testing was done in the period before publication in 2014\&. 
